WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.417 --> 00:00:02.251
<i>Previously on "The Ark"...</i>

2
00:00:02.252 --> 00:00:03.627
Their message sounded
like they're in trouble.

3
00:00:03.628 --> 00:00:05.212
<i>You're heading down there.
Is it safe?</i>

4
00:00:05.213 --> 00:00:07.506
-Of course it's safe.
<i>-They're all dead.</i>

5
00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.550
<i>Admiral Ben Hammond
of "Ark 4."</i>

6
00:00:09.551 --> 00:00:12.469
Meet Milan Petrovic.
head of Homebase 1 security.

7
00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:14.138
<i>I believe Kelly Fowler
should be freed.</i>

8
00:00:14.139 --> 00:00:15.889
<i>I have to go out
in the exploration zone.</i>

9
00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:17.933
<i>You want to come?</i>

10
00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:19.518
We're pinned down
and won't be able to make it

11
00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:21.311
-to the shuttle.
-"Pinned down"? By what?

12
00:00:21.312 --> 00:00:22.813
Alien bloody creatures. mate.

13
00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.025
I'm gonna pull 'em off this way.

14
00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:28.569
No!

15
00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:31.613
-Brice!
-Run!

16
00:00:31.614 --> 00:00:35.535
I'm so sorry. Eva.
but he's dead.

17
00:00:56.264 --> 00:00:58.307
I wish we had a funeral
for Lieutenant Brice

18
00:00:58.308 --> 00:01:01.518
like we did for Doc Morozov.

19
00:01:01.519 --> 00:01:03.354
Brice always thought
he was gonna die young

20
00:01:03.355 --> 00:01:06.023
from Klampkins and made it
very clear he didn't want us

21
00:01:06.024 --> 00:01:09.234
wallowing in grief for him.

22
00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:12.404
And yet here we are.

23
00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.948
Well. I mean. I didn't know
him as well as you lot did.

24
00:01:14.949 --> 00:01:17.576
but Brice always seemed like
a "raise a glass of scotch"

25
00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:21.330
-"and celebrate me" kind of guy.
-No. no.

26
00:01:21.331 --> 00:01:24.667
A whiskey from the homeland
tasted like piss.

27
00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:27.878
Which do you think
he hated more.

28
00:01:27.879 --> 00:01:30.047
Scotch or William Trust?

29
00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:39.556
<i>Hammond to senior staff.
Report to the bridge.</i>

30
00:01:39.557 --> 00:01:42.518
Can he do that.
just call a meeting?

31
00:01:42.519 --> 00:01:44.979
Apparently. he thinks he can.

32
00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:56.991
So I've been reviewing your logs

33
00:01:56.992 --> 00:01:58.785
and I...

34
00:02:02.205 --> 00:02:04.498
What are you looking at?

35
00:02:04.499 --> 00:02:05.874
Uh. sir.

36
00:02:10.088 --> 00:02:12.214
Sorry. it was
the only free cabin.

37
00:02:12.215 --> 00:02:14.216
Your lieutenant
was the same size.

38
00:02:14.217 --> 00:02:17.594
As I said. I read your logs.

39
00:02:17.595 --> 00:02:19.596
and I want to set course
for the Tyson system.

40
00:02:19.597 --> 00:02:22.266
Wait. hold on.
Who's in charge?

41
00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:24.560
Sharon. obviously.

42
00:02:24.561 --> 00:02:28.230
I respect your
field promotion. Captain.

43
00:02:28.231 --> 00:02:29.940
but I still outrank you.

44
00:02:29.941 --> 00:02:32.901
In what?
The GSA is gone.

45
00:02:32.902 --> 00:02:34.528
Excuse me?

46
00:02:34.529 --> 00:02:36.655
You know
the GSA charter. Admiral.

47
00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:39.616
It clearly states we were to
get humanity to new homeworlds

48
00:02:39.617 --> 00:02:42.745
and relinquish control
to civilian governance.

49
00:02:45.623 --> 00:02:47.624
Then how does this all work?

50
00:02:47.625 --> 00:02:52.171
"Ark 1" is crewed by a mix
of former GSA and EF volunteers

51
00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:54.715
who've chosen to follow
Captain Garnet.

52
00:02:54.716 --> 00:02:56.842
"Ark 1" is now
a Homebase 1 ship.

53
00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:58.761
not a GSA ship.

54
00:03:03.224 --> 00:03:05.017
I'm sorry I overstepped.

55
00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:07.145
-It won't happen again.
-Good.

56
00:03:09.064 --> 00:03:10.607
But if I may?

57
00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:15.402
Did you know that
when Evelyn Maddox fled

58
00:03:15.403 --> 00:03:18.030
Homebase 1. she set a course
in the shuttle nav system?

59
00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:19.323
Yes.

60
00:03:19.324 --> 00:03:20.949
So why haven't you investigated?

61
00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:23.160
I thought it was
more important to make contact

62
00:03:23.161 --> 00:03:24.328
with the Ross colony.

63
00:03:24.329 --> 00:03:26.372
Even though
I warned you not to come?

64
00:03:26.373 --> 00:03:28.332
Well. that's a weird way
to say thanks.

65
00:03:28.333 --> 00:03:30.417
"Ark 1's" mission
is to save people at risk

66
00:03:30.418 --> 00:03:32.002
and bring them to Homebase.

67
00:03:32.003 --> 00:03:33.420
Okay. and don't you think

68
00:03:33.421 --> 00:03:35.339
there might be people
where Maddox was going?

69
00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:37.174
Yeah. people
that want to kill us.

70
00:03:37.175 --> 00:03:40.344
Or people who are suffering.
just as the people of Homebase

71
00:03:40.345 --> 00:03:43.514
were suffering
before you intervened.

72
00:03:43.515 --> 00:03:46.142
So you want to investigate now?

73
00:03:49.187 --> 00:03:52.356
Tyson 5E.
It can't support life.

74
00:03:52.357 --> 00:03:54.817
So it's likely
a rendezvous point.

75
00:03:54.818 --> 00:03:56.068
Exactly.

76
00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:58.278
Whoever Maddox was meeting

77
00:03:58.279 --> 00:04:00.781
might still be there
waiting for her.

78
00:04:00.782 --> 00:04:04.326
We can drop out of FTL here.
right behind Tyson's moon.

79
00:04:04.327 --> 00:04:06.412
To hide us
from any ships in orbit.

80
00:04:06.413 --> 00:04:07.914
Solid plan.

81
00:04:11.376 --> 00:04:14.002
Okay. let's set a course.

82
00:04:19.134 --> 00:04:20.552
Admiral. a moment?

83
00:04:22.721 --> 00:04:25.514
You read my logs.
I read your files.

84
00:04:25.515 --> 00:04:27.516
I appreciate your experience.

85
00:04:27.517 --> 00:04:31.020
-But not enough to follow me?
-No.

86
00:04:31.021 --> 00:04:34.565
But you'd clearly be an asset.

87
00:04:34.566 --> 00:04:36.316
I could use a number two.

88
00:04:50.832 --> 00:04:52.291
Kelly?

89
00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:56.045
Where are...

90
00:04:56.046 --> 00:04:58.172
What am I wearing?

91
00:04:58.173 --> 00:05:00.132
I don't know.

92
00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:02.426
-You changed my clothes?
-No.

93
00:05:02.427 --> 00:05:04.428
I just woke up a minute ago.

94
00:05:05.847 --> 00:05:08.223
Why aren't you wearing
these weird clothes?

95
00:05:08.224 --> 00:05:10.059
Again. I don't know.

96
00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:11.477
We were in the woods.

97
00:05:11.478 --> 00:05:15.648
There was a flash of light.
and here we are.

98
00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:24.198
No signal.

99
00:05:24.199 --> 00:05:25.366
Okay.

100
00:05:29.204 --> 00:05:32.456
My implants are on. and
I'm not even making a scratch.

101
00:05:32.457 --> 00:05:35.417
There's no doors.
How did we get in here?

102
00:05:35.418 --> 00:05:37.211
What I want to know is...

103
00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:42.966
How do we get out?

104
00:06:02.904 --> 00:06:05.572
Captain Garnet.
Ian and I have a report on...

105
00:06:05.573 --> 00:06:08.033
Crewman. brief me first.

106
00:06:08.034 --> 00:06:09.576
-Oh.
-Seriously?

107
00:06:09.577 --> 00:06:11.704
Chain of command.

108
00:06:11.705 --> 00:06:14.873
As her second. it's my job to
make sure her life is easier.

109
00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:17.084
"Her second"?

110
00:06:17.085 --> 00:06:19.628
Thank you. but we do things
a little differently here.

111
00:06:19.629 --> 00:06:21.630
They can report to me directly.

112
00:06:21.631 --> 00:06:25.050
Captain. I gave up sunlight
and fresh air at Homebase

113
00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:27.386
-to take orders from you.
-And I'm still in command.

114
00:06:27.387 --> 00:06:31.057
But you gave Brice's job
to some guy who hitched a ride?

115
00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:37.438
Let's all remember.
the admiral earned his rank.

116
00:06:37.439 --> 00:06:41.025
We can benefit
from his experience.

117
00:06:41.026 --> 00:06:43.402
My training is
in peaceful missions.

118
00:06:43.403 --> 00:06:45.572
same as Captain Garnet.

119
00:06:47.657 --> 00:06:50.284
Is that good enough
for you. crewman?

120
00:06:56.624 --> 00:06:58.542
You have a report
for the captain?

121
00:06:58.543 --> 00:07:02.046
Oh. uh. yeah.
um. we've been analyzing

122
00:07:02.047 --> 00:07:04.006
the data on the solar shields
we created at Ross.

123
00:07:04.007 --> 00:07:05.674
I think we can make them
sustainable.

124
00:07:05.675 --> 00:07:07.051
Yeah. with a bit of work.

125
00:07:07.052 --> 00:07:08.844
we can calibrate them
to protect us

126
00:07:08.845 --> 00:07:10.512
from different wavelengths
of radiation

127
00:07:10.513 --> 00:07:12.139
and electromagnetic pulses.

128
00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:15.017
And maybe even small impacts
from solid matter

129
00:07:15.018 --> 00:07:16.477
like asteroid fragments.

130
00:07:16.478 --> 00:07:18.354
How about impact from artillery?

131
00:07:18.355 --> 00:07:20.481
Well. what ever happened
to peaceful missions?

132
00:07:20.482 --> 00:07:21.940
I want peace.

133
00:07:21.941 --> 00:07:24.110
Doesn't mean everyone else does.

134
00:07:37.457 --> 00:07:38.957
Uh-oh.

135
00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:40.209
I know that look.

136
00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:41.919
This?

137
00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:44.505
This is my normal.
handsome. everyday look.

138
00:07:44.506 --> 00:07:46.757
It's your
"dying to say something

139
00:07:46.758 --> 00:07:49.718
"but biting your tongue" look.

140
00:07:49.719 --> 00:07:51.303
No. it's not my place.

141
00:07:51.304 --> 00:07:53.097
I want to respect
your boundaries.

142
00:07:53.098 --> 00:07:57.059
Ha. says the man trying
to nickname me Curly

143
00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:58.727
because he dreamed it.

144
00:07:58.728 --> 00:08:02.398
Yeah. about that...

145
00:08:02.399 --> 00:08:04.108
I think I understand now

146
00:08:04.109 --> 00:08:07.903
why you think our time
in the coma wasn't real.

147
00:08:07.904 --> 00:08:11.031
I spent decades
learning astrophysics. right?

148
00:08:11.032 --> 00:08:13.409
Now it turns out
it was just my brain

149
00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:16.120
creating fake science.

150
00:08:16.121 --> 00:08:18.832
So what else
did my brain make up?

151
00:08:21.418 --> 00:08:23.669
I appreciate that.

152
00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:26.130
But I still want to know
what's on your mind.

153
00:08:26.131 --> 00:08:28.424
Isn't it obvious?

154
00:08:28.425 --> 00:08:29.883
I don't trust Hammond.

155
00:08:29.884 --> 00:08:31.760
Because he tried
to take command?

156
00:08:31.761 --> 00:08:34.888
Because he backed down
too easily.

157
00:08:34.889 --> 00:08:38.142
I mean. does that sound
like any admiral you ever met?

158
00:08:47.485 --> 00:08:52.156
Leaving FTL in three. two...

159
00:08:52.157 --> 00:08:54.408
now.

160
00:08:54.409 --> 00:08:57.870
Well. you cut that
a little close. Kimi.

161
00:08:57.871 --> 00:09:00.622
Plan called for us to get as
near to the moon as possible.

162
00:09:00.623 --> 00:09:02.124
And we got here in one piece.

163
00:09:02.125 --> 00:09:05.002
Call that good work.
Lieutenant Joma.

164
00:09:05.003 --> 00:09:07.004
Passive scans only. Alicia.

165
00:09:07.005 --> 00:09:10.382
Let's try not to alert anyone
to our presence.

166
00:09:10.383 --> 00:09:13.719
It might be
a little bit late for that.

167
00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:16.555
It's "Ark 22."
They have energy weapons.

168
00:09:16.556 --> 00:09:18.390
You remember what I said
about people

169
00:09:18.391 --> 00:09:20.559
-wanting to kill us?
-Can your shield stop them?

170
00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.561
No. we're still upgrading them.

171
00:09:22.562 --> 00:09:24.313
We're being hailed.

172
00:09:24.314 --> 00:09:25.564
Charge FTL fast.

173
00:09:25.565 --> 00:09:27.024
Send them to my screen.

174
00:09:32.364 --> 00:09:34.657
<i>Oh.</i>

175
00:09:34.658 --> 00:09:36.408
<i>Smart hiding place.</i>

176
00:09:36.409 --> 00:09:38.410
<i>Didn't work but smart.</i>

177
00:09:38.411 --> 00:09:41.038
<i>Let me guess... you're looking
for Evelyn Maddox?</i>

178
00:09:41.039 --> 00:09:42.039
Not exactly.

179
00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:44.041
I'm Captain Sharon Garnet
of "Ark 1."

180
00:09:44.042 --> 00:09:46.418
<i>Kurtis Drake.
leader of "Ark 22."</i>

181
00:09:46.419 --> 00:09:48.879
We were investigating
why Evelyn Maddox may...

182
00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:51.131
<i>You're a clone.</i>

183
00:09:51.132 --> 00:09:54.718
<i>you and the gentleman
at your side.</i>

184
00:09:54.719 --> 00:09:57.221
Uh. what makes you think
I'm a clone?

185
00:09:57.222 --> 00:10:00.766
<i>Well. because
I'm married to you.</i>

186
00:10:00.767 --> 00:10:05.187
<i>I'm married to one of you.</i>

187
00:10:05.188 --> 00:10:09.191
<i>-This is. um. Jill.
-Hi. there.</i>

188
00:10:09.192 --> 00:10:11.402
<i>Is it conceited to say
you're very beautiful?</i>

189
00:10:11.403 --> 00:10:15.948
<i>Even in those drab colors.</i>

190
00:10:15.949 --> 00:10:18.617
<i>Oh. and we do have J6-82s
on board as well.</i>

191
00:10:18.618 --> 00:10:21.870
<i>Richard. Clark. come and say hi.</i>

192
00:10:21.871 --> 00:10:24.540
<i>Oh.
Hello. brother.</i>

193
00:10:24.541 --> 00:10:25.749
<i>-Hey.
-Yeah.</i>

194
00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:27.626
Did you know there were
other clones of you?

195
00:10:27.627 --> 00:10:29.253
N...

196
00:10:29.254 --> 00:10:31.588
<i>Come on over.
It'd be lovely to have you.</i>

197
00:10:31.589 --> 00:10:34.508
No. we don't give up our people.

198
00:10:34.509 --> 00:10:38.262
<i>You misunderstand.
This is not a request.</i>

199
00:10:38.263 --> 00:10:41.181
He's charging weapons.

200
00:10:41.182 --> 00:10:42.808
<i>Fire on my mark.</i>

201
00:10:42.809 --> 00:10:46.311
<i>Three. two. one.</i>

202
00:10:46.312 --> 00:10:48.480
-All right. we'll go.
-We'll come. We'll come over.

203
00:10:48.481 --> 00:10:49.982
<i>Good.</i>

204
00:10:49.983 --> 00:10:51.650
<i>I look forward to it.</i>

205
00:10:51.651 --> 00:10:54.279
<i>Don't take too long.</i>

206
00:10:56.698 --> 00:10:59.616
No. you can't go over there.

207
00:10:59.617 --> 00:11:01.327
We don't have a choice.

208
00:11:03.413 --> 00:11:06.540
Admiral Hammond has command
while I'm gone.

209
00:11:06.541 --> 00:11:07.833
Really?

210
00:11:07.834 --> 00:11:10.586
Those are my orders.

211
00:11:10.587 --> 00:11:12.171
Keep this ship safe.

212
00:11:17.135 --> 00:11:19.178
This could be
a good thing. right?

213
00:11:19.179 --> 00:11:21.472
I mean. means there's
more of us in the universe.

214
00:11:21.473 --> 00:11:23.932
Who have a whole lot
of weapons pointed at us.

215
00:11:23.933 --> 00:11:26.019
Yeah. there is that.

216
00:11:27.771 --> 00:11:29.104
I don't like this.

217
00:11:29.105 --> 00:11:32.232
We should have hidden weapons
in the shuttle.

218
00:11:32.233 --> 00:11:34.777
Weapons or not.
they're outnumbered.

219
00:11:34.778 --> 00:11:36.820
<i>Clear of "Ark 1."</i>

220
00:11:36.821 --> 00:11:39.198
Godspeed. Captain.

221
00:11:39.199 --> 00:11:41.325
"Ark 1." out.

222
00:11:41.326 --> 00:11:45.537
Okay. so what's your plan
to get them home?

223
00:11:45.538 --> 00:11:47.581
Is the FTL charged?

224
00:11:47.582 --> 00:11:49.833
Yeah. but...

225
00:11:51.336 --> 00:11:55.547
Ugh.
I really don't like that guy.

226
00:12:23.201 --> 00:12:25.411
It's a little early. Felix.

227
00:12:25.412 --> 00:12:29.289
Yes. well. I've been trying
to reach you since last night.

228
00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:31.875
My WD is off.
What do you need?

229
00:12:31.876 --> 00:12:33.460
Um...

230
00:12:43.763 --> 00:12:46.140
You're watching video
of Brice's death?

231
00:12:46.141 --> 00:12:48.017
Garnet sent me the footage

232
00:12:48.018 --> 00:12:50.477
from the shuttle's hull cameras.

233
00:12:50.478 --> 00:12:51.813
Have you slept?

234
00:12:53.982 --> 00:12:56.400
Don't torture yourself
like this. Eva.

235
00:12:56.401 --> 00:12:58.819
I have to see it.

236
00:12:58.820 --> 00:13:01.530
May I ask you to take a break?

237
00:13:01.531 --> 00:13:04.074
I have something to show you.

238
00:13:04.075 --> 00:13:05.409
Please.

239
00:13:08.788 --> 00:13:11.623
-It's a new concept.
-Okay. what it is?

240
00:13:11.624 --> 00:13:12.917
There they are.

241
00:13:15.003 --> 00:13:16.253
Come here.

242
00:13:23.303 --> 00:13:25.012
I'm sorry.

243
00:13:28.808 --> 00:13:31.894
I don't normally like people
invading my personal space.

244
00:13:31.895 --> 00:13:34.229
However.
given the circumstances...

245
00:13:37.609 --> 00:13:40.194
He was a good man. I guess.

246
00:13:40.195 --> 00:13:43.155
So what did you have
to show me. Felix?

247
00:13:43.156 --> 00:13:45.240
That you are not alone.

248
00:13:47.952 --> 00:13:49.203
Thank you.

249
00:13:49.204 --> 00:13:50.537
Sit down.

250
00:13:54.167 --> 00:13:55.626
You eaten?

251
00:13:55.627 --> 00:13:58.295
-You should eat.
-Stop mothering her.

252
00:13:58.296 --> 00:14:00.130
I'm doctoring her.

253
00:14:00.131 --> 00:14:02.800
I could definitely eat.
Who are we waiting for?

254
00:14:02.801 --> 00:14:05.302
Angus.
I couldn't get a hold of him.

255
00:14:05.303 --> 00:14:06.595
Neither could I.

256
00:14:06.596 --> 00:14:08.138
Well. I'm not gonna
wait for him.

257
00:14:08.139 --> 00:14:10.182
I'm gonna go
and get some breakfast.

258
00:14:10.183 --> 00:14:12.142
You do that.

259
00:14:12.143 --> 00:14:14.813
Hey. you want some coffee?

260
00:14:18.191 --> 00:14:21.819
Who do you think put us here?

261
00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:24.196
I'm more worried
about what put us here.

262
00:14:24.197 --> 00:14:25.239
Yeah. you have a point.

263
00:14:25.240 --> 00:14:26.990
These walls are too smooth
to be natural.

264
00:14:26.991 --> 00:14:28.909
They had to have been
machine-honed.

265
00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:31.912
which means someone
pretty advanced built these.

266
00:14:31.913 --> 00:14:35.999
God. I just... I wonder about
the light from these crystals.

267
00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:38.502
Is it electric.
naturally occurring.

268
00:14:38.503 --> 00:14:40.254
filtered through
from some different...

269
00:14:40.255 --> 00:14:41.714
Can you stop that?

270
00:14:41.715 --> 00:14:43.465
You said it's not making a dent.

271
00:14:43.466 --> 00:14:45.093
Kelly. I said stop...

272
00:14:46.886 --> 00:14:50.557
Man. Kelly.
you're trashing your hand.

273
00:14:53.184 --> 00:14:55.811
It doesn't hurt that much.

274
00:14:55.812 --> 00:14:58.981
You're obviously in pain.
Take a break.

275
00:14:58.982 --> 00:15:02.234
It's not my hand that hurts.
It's my ears.

276
00:15:02.235 --> 00:15:05.195
With my implants on.
I hear this awful noise.

277
00:15:05.196 --> 00:15:06.447
Turn the implants off.

278
00:15:06.448 --> 00:15:08.407
Besides. you don't want to go
into organ failure.

279
00:15:08.408 --> 00:15:12.036
Whoever took us will be back.
I need to be ready to fight.

280
00:15:12.037 --> 00:15:14.663
I'll fight them off till
you get your implants back on.

281
00:15:14.664 --> 00:15:18.208
That's funny.

282
00:15:18.209 --> 00:15:20.294
Oh. you're serious.

283
00:15:20.295 --> 00:15:22.254
Turn them off.

284
00:15:25.633 --> 00:15:27.343
Better?

285
00:15:27.344 --> 00:15:29.136
I guess.

286
00:15:29.137 --> 00:15:31.805
At least I'm not hearing
that screeching sound anymore.

287
00:15:36.519 --> 00:15:39.480
Something's wrong.

288
00:15:39.481 --> 00:15:41.357
I'm still hearing those sounds.

289
00:15:41.358 --> 00:15:44.234
Wait. I hear them. too. now.

290
00:15:44.235 --> 00:15:47.821
Wait. That's what they sounded
like with your implants on?

291
00:15:47.822 --> 00:15:50.532
It's not that bad.

292
00:15:50.533 --> 00:15:53.160
Aah!

293
00:15:53.161 --> 00:15:54.996
Ah. strike that.

294
00:15:59.459 --> 00:16:02.169
And so I think we should take
a moment of silence

295
00:16:02.170 --> 00:16:05.381
for James Brice
and Dr. Morozov.

296
00:16:11.554 --> 00:16:13.639
Now we must move forward.

297
00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:17.142
I'm afraid we have
some more troubling news.

298
00:16:17.143 --> 00:16:20.854
Two of Homebase 1's citizens
are missing.

299
00:16:20.855 --> 00:16:24.900
Angus Medford and Kelly Fowler
went to the expanded zone

300
00:16:24.901 --> 00:16:26.193
and never returned.

301
00:16:26.194 --> 00:16:27.736
We lost contact.

302
00:16:27.737 --> 00:16:29.863
You know what probably happened.

303
00:16:29.864 --> 00:16:32.157
Kelly went psycho
and killed her ex-boyfriend.

304
00:16:32.158 --> 00:16:34.034
Let's not jump to conclusions.

305
00:16:34.035 --> 00:16:36.870
I spent 3 years
on "Ark 15" with her.

306
00:16:36.871 --> 00:16:39.581
-We can't trust her.
-It's true!

307
00:16:41.292 --> 00:16:42.668
Stop.

308
00:16:42.669 --> 00:16:46.255
These speculations
about Ms. Fowler end now.

309
00:16:46.256 --> 00:16:48.549
She's proven herself repeatedly.

310
00:16:48.550 --> 00:16:51.468
What's important
is to find them.

311
00:16:51.469 --> 00:16:54.347
I'm taking volunteers
for a search party.

312
00:16:56.766 --> 00:16:58.142
Thank you.

313
00:16:58.143 --> 00:17:00.769
We'll leave after
our last order of business.

314
00:17:00.770 --> 00:17:03.480
It's no secret that.
with the arrival

315
00:17:03.481 --> 00:17:06.400
of "Ark 1" and "EF2."

316
00:17:06.401 --> 00:17:10.988
has led to some growing
problems in our colony.

317
00:17:10.989 --> 00:17:15.743
Our council has appointed
a new sheriff. Milan Petrovic.

318
00:17:19.873 --> 00:17:24.626
Some of you worked
with Milan on "Ark 11"

319
00:17:24.627 --> 00:17:26.378
when he was head of security.

320
00:17:26.379 --> 00:17:29.882
We're sure that he will do
as well at this position.

321
00:17:45.523 --> 00:17:47.524
Sanji?
Sanji. what's wrong?

322
00:17:47.525 --> 00:17:49.943
-It's him.
-Him... who?

323
00:17:49.944 --> 00:17:51.737
-The sheriff.
-What?

324
00:17:51.738 --> 00:17:53.948
He's my ex-husband.

325
00:17:58.703 --> 00:18:00.579
Hey. hey. are you crazy?

326
00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:01.955
Sanji. I'm gonna talk to him.

327
00:18:01.956 --> 00:18:03.207
-No.
-Sanji!

328
00:18:03.208 --> 00:18:05.626
No. I need to handle
this myself.

329
00:18:05.627 --> 00:18:07.252
No. I'll go.
I'll talk to him.

330
00:18:07.253 --> 00:18:09.881
Just give me a moment to think.

331
00:18:12.467 --> 00:18:15.052
-Hello. Sanji.
-Stay away from her.

332
00:18:15.053 --> 00:18:17.888
-Damir.
-Let me talk to him.

333
00:18:17.889 --> 00:18:19.598
-I'll handle this.
-Sanji.

334
00:18:19.599 --> 00:18:20.975
Alone!

335
00:18:22.811 --> 00:18:24.228
Okay.

336
00:18:24.229 --> 00:18:26.522
I'll be in the dorm
if you need me.

337
00:18:33.613 --> 00:18:36.074
It's good to see you.

338
00:18:38.493 --> 00:18:42.496
Um. can we talk somewhere
more private?

339
00:18:42.497 --> 00:18:44.623
Here's fine.

340
00:18:44.624 --> 00:18:47.459
Fair enough.
Um...

341
00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:49.420
I owe you an apology.

342
00:18:52.799 --> 00:18:55.342
I'm sober now.

343
00:18:55.343 --> 00:18:59.471
I know that doesn't excuse
anything. but...

344
00:18:59.472 --> 00:19:03.392
I want you to know
I'm not the man I was.

345
00:19:03.393 --> 00:19:06.520
Good.

346
00:19:06.521 --> 00:19:10.607
I'm not the woman I was either.

347
00:19:10.608 --> 00:19:13.153
So leave me the hell alone.

348
00:19:33.173 --> 00:19:37.801
If you go near Sanji
ever again. I will end you.

349
00:19:37.802 --> 00:19:40.763
You hear me. you piece of shit?

350
00:19:40.764 --> 00:19:43.724
Loud and clear.

351
00:19:43.725 --> 00:19:46.477
What. you gonna hit me.
or you gonna let me go?

352
00:19:46.478 --> 00:19:48.604
What's it gonna be. hmm?

353
00:19:53.818 --> 00:19:55.736
Good to meet you. Damir.

354
00:20:09.167 --> 00:20:11.460
For someone so concerned
with GSA protocols...

355
00:20:11.461 --> 00:20:13.461
I can't believe you just
deserted Captain Garnet...

356
00:20:14.798 --> 00:20:16.715
That's a direct violation
of GSA codes.

357
00:20:16.716 --> 00:20:19.385
I guarantee you
no one will stand for it.

358
00:20:19.386 --> 00:20:22.096
Are you finished. or are you
just taking a breath?

359
00:20:22.097 --> 00:20:24.056
How can you joke right now?

360
00:20:24.057 --> 00:20:26.433
I'm actually trying
to keep my patience

361
00:20:26.434 --> 00:20:28.602
as you voice your concerns.

362
00:20:28.603 --> 00:20:30.979
You abandoned
Captain Garnet and Ian.

363
00:20:30.980 --> 00:20:33.107
You heard the Captain's orders.

364
00:20:33.108 --> 00:20:37.194
-She said keep the ship safe.
-Yeah. not run away.

365
00:20:37.195 --> 00:20:39.738
Ms. Nevins. your shields
still aren't repaired.

366
00:20:39.739 --> 00:20:41.615
What does that
have to do with...

367
00:20:41.616 --> 00:20:43.283
And we don't have any weapons.

368
00:20:43.284 --> 00:20:45.452
-We weren't under attack.
-Drake had what he wanted.

369
00:20:45.453 --> 00:20:47.705
There was no reason to assume
that he wouldn't open up fire.

370
00:20:47.706 --> 00:20:49.581
And there's no reason
to assume that he would.

371
00:20:49.582 --> 00:20:52.084
I won't risk the lives of
the entire ship for two people!

372
00:20:52.085 --> 00:20:54.336
We just risked this entire
ship to save you on Ross.

373
00:20:54.337 --> 00:20:55.921
And that was a bad move!

374
00:20:55.922 --> 00:20:58.799
You lost your doctor
and your number two.

375
00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:01.135
The math doesn't work.

376
00:21:01.136 --> 00:21:04.638
People aren't math.

377
00:21:04.639 --> 00:21:06.725
Sometimes they are.

378
00:21:10.562 --> 00:21:14.273
On Ross. Garnet traded
two lives to save one.

379
00:21:14.274 --> 00:21:16.817
Math.

380
00:21:16.818 --> 00:21:18.652
She put me in charge
because she knew

381
00:21:18.653 --> 00:21:20.487
I wouldn't make
the same mistake.

382
00:21:20.488 --> 00:21:23.782
Or you're happy she's gone...

383
00:21:23.783 --> 00:21:26.243
so you can have this ship.

384
00:21:28.121 --> 00:21:31.165
Given the stress
of what's happened.

385
00:21:31.166 --> 00:21:33.959
I'm gonna pretend
I didn't hear that...

386
00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:35.544
Lieutenant Joma.

387
00:21:47.098 --> 00:21:49.058
Thank you so much
for coming over.

388
00:21:49.059 --> 00:21:51.185
Yeah. well.
we didn't have a choice.

389
00:21:51.186 --> 00:21:52.770
I never would have fired.

390
00:21:52.771 --> 00:21:55.272
Yeah. but sometimes
a show of force keeps people

391
00:21:55.273 --> 00:21:57.191
from getting the wrong idea.

392
00:21:57.192 --> 00:21:59.693
Oh. I see.
and the armed guards...

393
00:21:59.694 --> 00:22:02.196
what kind of idea is
that supposed to give us?

394
00:22:02.197 --> 00:22:04.114
Oh. just a precaution.

395
00:22:04.115 --> 00:22:06.700
I-I wanted to greet you
privately.

396
00:22:06.701 --> 00:22:10.204
but my wife...
yeah. she worries.

397
00:22:10.205 --> 00:22:12.581
WDs. please.

398
00:22:12.582 --> 00:22:14.124
Is that necessary?

399
00:22:14.125 --> 00:22:17.045
We'll keep them safe
in our security lockup.

400
00:22:25.261 --> 00:22:27.930
-Can you roll up your sleeves?
-Back off.

401
00:22:27.931 --> 00:22:31.266
It's okay.
We don't use J6-82s for organs.

402
00:22:31.267 --> 00:22:34.687
-I have a name. and it's Ian.
-Excellent.

403
00:22:34.688 --> 00:22:36.313
I encourage you even
to take a last name.

404
00:22:36.314 --> 00:22:37.773
What's that for?

405
00:22:37.774 --> 00:22:40.317
We need blood samples
to make sure you're not Gen-3s.

406
00:22:40.318 --> 00:22:41.735
Well. we're not.

407
00:22:41.736 --> 00:22:44.071
Otherwise. we would have
already developed psychosis.

408
00:22:44.072 --> 00:22:45.280
That's not true.

409
00:22:45.281 --> 00:22:47.866
There are the occasional
late bloomers.

410
00:22:47.867 --> 00:22:50.160
Easy way or hard way...
up to you.

411
00:22:54.749 --> 00:22:57.292
You two don't seem to know
much about clone science.

412
00:22:57.293 --> 00:22:58.585
We know enough.

413
00:22:58.586 --> 00:23:00.379
Original humans
are Generation 1.

414
00:23:00.380 --> 00:23:01.755
and us clones are Gen-2s.

415
00:23:01.756 --> 00:23:04.174
And clones made
from Gen-2 DNA are Gen-3.

416
00:23:04.175 --> 00:23:05.300
Very good.

417
00:23:05.301 --> 00:23:08.679
And Gen-3 brain cells
are unstable.

418
00:23:08.680 --> 00:23:11.306
and they do develop psychosis.

419
00:23:11.307 --> 00:23:12.599
They're dangerous.

420
00:23:12.600 --> 00:23:14.727
which is why we have
to make sure you aren't one.

421
00:23:14.728 --> 00:23:16.687
How do you know Evelyn Maddox?

422
00:23:16.688 --> 00:23:18.647
Evelyn was
a business acquaintance.

423
00:23:18.648 --> 00:23:21.817
She sold me this Ark
during Earth's last days.

424
00:23:21.818 --> 00:23:25.029
Joke's on her.
What does money matter now?

425
00:23:25.030 --> 00:23:27.531
-Why were you meeting her?
-I have no idea.

426
00:23:27.532 --> 00:23:31.452
She called me. but something
tells me she. um...

427
00:23:31.453 --> 00:23:33.912
she won't be showing up
just now. will she?

428
00:23:33.913 --> 00:23:35.789
You could have told
us that over comms.

429
00:23:35.790 --> 00:23:37.624
Well. then I wouldn't have
the pleasure

430
00:23:37.625 --> 00:23:39.376
to meet you lovelies in person.

431
00:23:39.377 --> 00:23:40.627
What do you want from us?

432
00:23:40.628 --> 00:23:42.796
It's not what I want from you.

433
00:23:42.797 --> 00:23:44.423
It's what you want from me.

434
00:23:50.764 --> 00:23:53.932
-Ian?
-Oh. I see it.

435
00:23:53.933 --> 00:23:55.809
I don't quite believe it.

436
00:23:55.810 --> 00:23:57.978
This ship is a safe haven
for clones.

437
00:23:57.979 --> 00:24:00.815
Wait. are you saying everyone
on this ship is a clone?

438
00:24:02.984 --> 00:24:04.985
It's great. isn't it?

439
00:24:04.986 --> 00:24:08.238
Guys. how are you?

440
00:24:08.239 --> 00:24:10.157
-Thank you so much for dinner.
-Ah!

441
00:24:10.158 --> 00:24:12.993
No. it was delicious.
It was perfect.

442
00:24:12.994 --> 00:24:15.621
I never imagined
so many clones survived Earth.

443
00:24:15.622 --> 00:24:17.456
It's amazing.

444
00:24:17.457 --> 00:24:19.958
Yeah. I mean. besides
my brothers in the lab.

445
00:24:19.959 --> 00:24:22.169
I've never even met
another clone like me.

446
00:24:22.170 --> 00:24:25.130
Same. I always thought
it was just me and Denise.

447
00:24:25.131 --> 00:24:28.050
I wonder how many
of each Gen-2 models were made.

448
00:24:28.051 --> 00:24:29.301
A lot.

449
00:24:29.302 --> 00:24:31.845
The original humans designed
clones to be exploited...

450
00:24:31.846 --> 00:24:34.139
you know. labor. parts. experimentation.

451
00:24:34.140 --> 00:24:36.058
So they wouldn't go
to all that expense

452
00:24:36.059 --> 00:24:38.102
-only to create a few of us.
-That's right.

453
00:24:38.103 --> 00:24:40.562
Cloning was a business.
and if they hadn't cut corners

454
00:24:40.563 --> 00:24:42.189
by using Gen-2s
to create Gen-3s.

455
00:24:42.190 --> 00:24:44.024
the business
would have never been outlawed.

456
00:24:44.025 --> 00:24:45.734
I do have to admit.
it does make a nice change

457
00:24:45.735 --> 00:24:47.820
to see clones walking around
with smiles on their faces.

458
00:24:47.821 --> 00:24:49.905
So this is the part
where you thank me

459
00:24:49.906 --> 00:24:52.574
-for saving you from that ship.
-Saving us?

460
00:24:52.575 --> 00:24:54.243
She was the freaking captain.

461
00:24:54.244 --> 00:24:55.911
Of a GSA Ark?

462
00:24:55.912 --> 00:24:57.913
They haven't exactly been allies

463
00:24:57.914 --> 00:24:59.289
to the clone cause. have they?

464
00:24:59.290 --> 00:25:01.166
The GSA doesn't exist
anymore. mate.

465
00:25:01.167 --> 00:25:03.502
We've got a new colony now.
Homebase 1.

466
00:25:03.503 --> 00:25:06.130
It's pretty nice. too.
and clones are welcome there.

467
00:25:06.131 --> 00:25:08.257
And valued.
just like anyone else.

468
00:25:08.258 --> 00:25:10.801
just like we are welcome
on "Ark 1."

469
00:25:10.802 --> 00:25:13.262
Oh. okay.

470
00:25:13.263 --> 00:25:15.472
Then why did they
leave you behind?

471
00:25:25.483 --> 00:25:27.234
Working on a rescue plan?

472
00:25:27.235 --> 00:25:29.403
If the admiral wants math.
I'll give him math.

473
00:25:29.404 --> 00:25:32.406
I've served under men
like Hammond before.

474
00:25:32.407 --> 00:25:34.408
He's not changing his mind.

475
00:25:34.409 --> 00:25:37.161
I wish Lieutenant Brice
was still here.

476
00:25:37.162 --> 00:25:39.538
What gives him the right
to decide how we proceed?

477
00:25:39.539 --> 00:25:42.249
Garnet did
when she left him in charge.

478
00:25:42.250 --> 00:25:46.003
Well. he'll change
his tune when I show him this.

479
00:25:46.004 --> 00:25:49.548
I hope so.
but. um. just in case...

480
00:25:49.549 --> 00:25:51.176
here's a plan B.

481
00:25:53.136 --> 00:25:55.513
It's always good to have
a backup plan.

482
00:25:57.891 --> 00:25:59.892
Are you searching
for inhabitable worlds

483
00:25:59.893 --> 00:26:01.185
to settle on?

484
00:26:01.186 --> 00:26:03.354
Who's to say
we haven't found one?

485
00:26:03.355 --> 00:26:06.273
-Is that your old man?
-Oh. no. no.

486
00:26:06.274 --> 00:26:08.734
That's. um. Kurtis Drake prime.

487
00:26:08.735 --> 00:26:11.362
the inventor of cloning science.

488
00:26:11.363 --> 00:26:14.323
But in a way. he's the...
he's the father of us all.

489
00:26:14.324 --> 00:26:16.200
You're his clone.

490
00:26:16.201 --> 00:26:20.454
Yes. uh. but do not mistake
my work for the creator's.

491
00:26:20.455 --> 00:26:23.832
-He sought wealth.
-And what do you seek?

492
00:26:23.833 --> 00:26:26.502
To build a place
for us to live in harmony

493
00:26:26.503 --> 00:26:29.755
without oppression
from the original humans.

494
00:26:29.756 --> 00:26:31.423
Clone society.

495
00:26:31.424 --> 00:26:34.760
Well. forget the fact
that your model was designed

496
00:26:34.761 --> 00:26:36.470
for the rigors of space

497
00:26:36.471 --> 00:26:38.681
or that you were made
to be an organ donor.

498
00:26:38.682 --> 00:26:40.808
Here we can be
whatever we want...

499
00:26:40.809 --> 00:26:43.769
doctors. scientists. poets.

500
00:26:43.770 --> 00:26:47.481
Here we're free.

501
00:26:47.482 --> 00:26:49.566
We have a colony you could join.

502
00:26:49.567 --> 00:26:52.945
I mean. the two of you might
be accepted. but all of us?

503
00:26:52.946 --> 00:26:55.698
Old prejudices die hard.
Captain.

504
00:26:55.699 --> 00:26:58.742
<i>Morgan to Drake.
Can you come to medbay?</i>

505
00:26:58.743 --> 00:27:00.953
On my way. Doctor.

506
00:27:00.954 --> 00:27:03.664
Oh. here's the mess hall.

507
00:27:03.665 --> 00:27:05.249
The food is delicious.

508
00:27:05.250 --> 00:27:07.459
Go on in. Relax.
Have a meal.

509
00:27:07.460 --> 00:27:09.420
I'm sure you'll have
more questions later.

510
00:27:09.421 --> 00:27:12.090
-No guards?
-We have nothing to hide.

511
00:27:27.439 --> 00:27:29.606
Uh...

512
00:27:44.372 --> 00:27:47.625
-I figured it out.
-You figured out what?

513
00:27:49.544 --> 00:27:51.378
There are a lot
of calculations on here

514
00:27:51.379 --> 00:27:53.255
that fall outside
of my expertise.

515
00:27:53.256 --> 00:27:56.675
Alicia has a plan to save
Captain Garnet and Ian.

516
00:27:56.676 --> 00:27:58.635
Oh.
I'm listening.

517
00:27:58.636 --> 00:28:01.555
A while ago. William Trust
created a weaponized EM pulse.

518
00:28:01.556 --> 00:28:03.599
According to your logs.
it nearly fried your engines.

519
00:28:03.600 --> 00:28:06.185
Yes. but I figured out
how to re-create it

520
00:28:06.186 --> 00:28:08.729
in a way that we can fire off
three shots safely.

521
00:28:08.730 --> 00:28:11.315
Wow.
Three shots.

522
00:28:11.316 --> 00:28:12.816
And what about your shields?

523
00:28:12.817 --> 00:28:14.234
Have you found a way

524
00:28:14.235 --> 00:28:16.403
to recalibrate them
to withstand "Ark 22" weapons?

525
00:28:16.404 --> 00:28:18.238
-No. but...
-All right. stop.

526
00:28:18.239 --> 00:28:19.990
But if the EM
disables their weapons...

527
00:28:19.991 --> 00:28:21.492
You're dismissed.

528
00:28:21.493 --> 00:28:24.286
Sir. no one is happy we've
left two of our own behind.

529
00:28:24.287 --> 00:28:25.788
We've had this conversation.

530
00:28:25.789 --> 00:28:28.374
I'm not gonna risk the lives
of the entire ship on an if.

531
00:28:28.375 --> 00:28:31.001
-Is this your final decision?
-Yes. it's my final decision.

532
00:28:31.002 --> 00:28:33.295
Now. unless you can...

533
00:28:36.800 --> 00:28:39.968
I was really hoping
we wouldn't have to do plan B.

534
00:28:43.765 --> 00:28:48.560
No one in or out until
we've got our captain back.

535
00:28:51.606 --> 00:28:53.524
Time is not on our side.

536
00:28:53.525 --> 00:28:55.484
If Kelly and Angus
suffered an accident.

537
00:28:55.485 --> 00:28:57.695
they'll need food. water.
and medical attention.

538
00:28:57.696 --> 00:28:59.906
We should pair up
and widen our search.

539
00:29:02.283 --> 00:29:04.743
I'll search with you. Felix.

540
00:29:04.744 --> 00:29:07.204
I think not.

541
00:29:09.040 --> 00:29:11.834
Who told you. Sanji or Marsh?

542
00:29:11.835 --> 00:29:13.919
I would have never approved
you as sheriff

543
00:29:13.920 --> 00:29:15.379
if I'd known who you are.

544
00:29:15.380 --> 00:29:17.506
Who I am. Felix.

545
00:29:17.507 --> 00:29:21.719
is a guy who wants to help
you find two missing people.

546
00:29:21.720 --> 00:29:23.387
Hey.

547
00:29:23.388 --> 00:29:26.098
Do you want my help or not?

548
00:29:38.695 --> 00:29:42.032
This is a torture technique.

549
00:29:43.700 --> 00:29:46.326
My WD is picking up patterns
in the noise.

550
00:29:46.327 --> 00:29:48.495
There's harmonic variations
at frequencies

551
00:29:48.496 --> 00:29:50.289
outside the range
of human hearing.

552
00:29:50.290 --> 00:29:51.832
So what does that mean?

553
00:29:51.833 --> 00:29:53.959
It explains
why you could hear it

554
00:29:53.960 --> 00:29:57.796
-when your implants were on.
-How is that helpful?

555
00:29:57.797 --> 00:30:00.591
I have no idea.

556
00:30:00.592 --> 00:30:02.719
I don't know.
I don't know.

557
00:30:18.902 --> 00:30:21.236
Oh. Markovic.
I'm glad you're here.

558
00:30:21.237 --> 00:30:23.947
I could use your help
to recalibrate the spectrograph

559
00:30:23.948 --> 00:30:26.617
to run a chemical analysis
on the tablet.

560
00:30:26.618 --> 00:30:29.828
Maybe later.

561
00:30:29.829 --> 00:30:31.205
This tablet

562
00:30:31.206 --> 00:30:34.041
could be the greatest discovery
of our lifetime.

563
00:30:34.042 --> 00:30:35.668
maybe human history.

564
00:30:35.669 --> 00:30:38.672
So what could possibly be
more interesting than that?

565
00:30:40.965 --> 00:30:43.467
Well...

566
00:30:43.468 --> 00:30:45.344
maybe working on the tablet

567
00:30:45.345 --> 00:30:47.179
will help take your mind
off your grief.

568
00:30:47.180 --> 00:30:50.516
Something happened to Brice
as the shuttle took off.

569
00:30:50.517 --> 00:30:53.727
-Eva.
-Just watch.

570
00:30:53.728 --> 00:30:56.689
First. an exhaust fume.

571
00:30:56.690 --> 00:30:58.732
and there. he's gone.

572
00:30:58.733 --> 00:31:00.734
I don't want to be harsh.

573
00:31:00.735 --> 00:31:03.696
but. uh. something
was eating him.

574
00:31:03.697 --> 00:31:06.615
-Then where is his body?
-I don't know.

575
00:31:06.616 --> 00:31:09.451
I guess the creature
dragged it away?

576
00:31:09.452 --> 00:31:13.872
Or he... he walked away.

577
00:31:13.873 --> 00:31:16.083
Eva...

578
00:31:16.084 --> 00:31:17.626
I understand.

579
00:31:17.627 --> 00:31:19.002
I really do.

580
00:31:19.003 --> 00:31:22.172
I desperately miss
Helena and Cat.

581
00:31:22.173 --> 00:31:24.842
but I've had to accept
that they're gone.

582
00:31:24.843 --> 00:31:27.553
just like you have to accept
that Lieutenant Brice is gone.

583
00:31:27.554 --> 00:31:29.596
Now. come on.

584
00:31:29.597 --> 00:31:32.391
Come and help me
with the tablet. please?

585
00:31:32.392 --> 00:31:33.600
No.

586
00:31:48.825 --> 00:31:51.410
Sun's getting low.
and it's still hot as hell.

587
00:31:51.411 --> 00:31:52.703
Everyone's exhausted.

588
00:31:52.704 --> 00:31:55.080
We can't stop
until we find them.

589
00:31:55.081 --> 00:31:56.373
Look. I get it.

590
00:31:56.374 --> 00:31:58.250
Angus and Kelly are your people.

591
00:31:58.251 --> 00:32:01.837
-but we've been at this all day.
-They're <i>our</i> people.

592
00:32:01.838 --> 00:32:03.547
Sure.

593
00:32:03.548 --> 00:32:04.965
But so are they.

594
00:32:04.966 --> 00:32:07.051
Look. everyone here needs a meal

595
00:32:07.052 --> 00:32:08.135
and a good night's sleep.

596
00:32:08.136 --> 00:32:10.179
We can continue
the search tomorrow.

597
00:32:10.180 --> 00:32:12.973
Come on. man.
tell me you're not tired.

598
00:32:12.974 --> 00:32:16.686
I'm going to keep on looking.
You can do what you want.

599
00:32:18.730 --> 00:32:22.274
Well. you're a better man
than me. Felix.

600
00:32:22.275 --> 00:32:24.902
Okay. everyone who's ready
to call it for the night.

601
00:32:24.903 --> 00:32:26.236
follow me.

602
00:32:35.830 --> 00:32:38.082
I can't take much more of this!

603
00:32:38.083 --> 00:32:39.208
What?

604
00:32:39.209 --> 00:32:41.460
I said. I can't take
more of this!

605
00:32:41.461 --> 00:32:43.003
Me either!

606
00:32:52.472 --> 00:32:54.724
Maybe someone heard us?

607
00:32:56.643 --> 00:32:59.103
Or the next torture
is about to begin.

608
00:33:03.733 --> 00:33:06.110
Get behind me.

609
00:33:09.531 --> 00:33:11.740
Maybe we're supposed to go out?

610
00:33:11.741 --> 00:33:13.951
It could be a trap.

611
00:33:33.471 --> 00:33:35.681
-Oh. shit.
-Angus!

612
00:33:42.689 --> 00:33:45.650
Maybe let's stay in here.

613
00:33:55.952 --> 00:33:57.786
Welcome aboard.

614
00:33:57.787 --> 00:33:59.329
-Ah.
-Thank you.

615
00:33:59.330 --> 00:34:01.165
Happy to be here.

616
00:34:01.166 --> 00:34:03.083
Something's wrong here. right?

617
00:34:03.084 --> 00:34:05.335
Yeah. Drake's pushing the
hard sell a little too much.

618
00:34:05.336 --> 00:34:07.171
Hey. girl!

619
00:34:07.172 --> 00:34:09.631
I've totally got clothes
in your size

620
00:34:09.632 --> 00:34:12.384
if you. like.
ever want to borrow them.

621
00:34:12.385 --> 00:34:14.511
Uh. y-you know I do.

622
00:34:14.512 --> 00:34:16.680
I knew it.

623
00:34:18.850 --> 00:34:21.060
Have you noticed there's
no other clones of Drake here.

624
00:34:21.061 --> 00:34:22.311
but there are of everyone else?

625
00:34:22.312 --> 00:34:23.771
Yeah. we're gonna need

626
00:34:23.772 --> 00:34:25.564
to figure out
his connection to Maddox.

627
00:34:25.565 --> 00:34:27.483
get our WDs.
and signal "Ark 1."

628
00:34:27.484 --> 00:34:28.984
You don't really believe

629
00:34:28.985 --> 00:34:30.778
we can rely on Hammond for help?

630
00:34:30.779 --> 00:34:32.279
If we can make contact.

631
00:34:32.280 --> 00:34:34.114
uh. maybe we can figure out
a rescue plan

632
00:34:34.115 --> 00:34:35.741
that won't put "Ark 1"
in danger.

633
00:34:35.742 --> 00:34:37.493
Fair enough.

634
00:34:37.494 --> 00:34:39.286
Divide and conquer?

635
00:34:39.287 --> 00:34:41.288
Yes. I'll get
into the security lockup

636
00:34:41.289 --> 00:34:42.665
and grab our WDs.

637
00:34:42.666 --> 00:34:44.249
Right. I'll go
to the server room.

638
00:34:44.250 --> 00:34:46.001
see if there's
any communications logs

639
00:34:46.002 --> 00:34:47.461
-with Maddox.
-I don't know.

640
00:34:47.462 --> 00:34:50.381
Going to the bridge
might look suspicious.

641
00:34:50.382 --> 00:34:52.591
What about Drake's quarters?

642
00:34:52.592 --> 00:34:55.594
Maybe there's a WD there
with some information on it.

643
00:34:55.595 --> 00:34:57.012
Good idea.

644
00:34:57.013 --> 00:34:58.848
-Meet at the shuttle.
-Yeah.

645
00:35:03.895 --> 00:35:05.562
What have you got for me?

646
00:35:05.563 --> 00:35:08.315
I ran the blood sample
three times.

647
00:35:10.694 --> 00:35:15.197
We finally found
what we were looking for.

648
00:35:38.388 --> 00:35:40.681
-You're not Clark.
-Uh. yes. I am.

649
00:35:40.682 --> 00:35:43.308
No. you're not.

650
00:35:43.309 --> 00:35:46.520
No. I'm not.

651
00:35:46.521 --> 00:35:49.273
You're one of the clones
Kurtis freed from "Ark 1."

652
00:35:49.274 --> 00:35:51.317
"Freed"?

653
00:35:51.318 --> 00:35:53.361
Kidnapped. more like.

654
00:35:55.572 --> 00:35:57.364
Oh. no.

655
00:35:57.365 --> 00:35:59.616
No. I wouldn't do that
if I was you.

656
00:35:59.617 --> 00:36:01.785
Kurtis is gonna throw
your ass out the airlock

657
00:36:01.786 --> 00:36:04.872
-for sneaking into our quarters.
-Oh. yeah?

658
00:36:04.873 --> 00:36:07.708
And tell me. what do you think
would make Drake angrier...

659
00:36:07.709 --> 00:36:09.043
me sneaking in here

660
00:36:09.044 --> 00:36:13.630
or you dressed like that
waiting for a guy named Clark?

661
00:36:17.093 --> 00:36:18.761
What do you want?

662
00:36:18.762 --> 00:36:21.430
What's Drake's connection
to Maddox?

663
00:36:21.431 --> 00:36:24.391
You tell me that.
and I'll leave.

664
00:36:24.392 --> 00:36:26.977
All's I know is Maddox
was trying to help Kurtis

665
00:36:26.978 --> 00:36:28.812
find a special G-44?

666
00:36:28.813 --> 00:36:30.647
What's a G-44?

667
00:36:33.360 --> 00:36:35.195
You're looking at one.

668
00:36:37.405 --> 00:36:40.241
Ship full of us
and still not the one he wants.

669
00:36:42.118 --> 00:36:45.245
Sharon.

670
00:36:50.418 --> 00:36:54.922
Oh. and you must be
the new G-44 clone.

671
00:36:54.923 --> 00:36:57.341
I'm Roger.

672
00:36:57.342 --> 00:36:59.886
Nice to meet you.

673
00:37:02.889 --> 00:37:05.057
Do you want to go
for a drink sometime?

674
00:37:05.058 --> 00:37:06.683
Excuse me?

675
00:37:06.684 --> 00:37:09.228
It's just that I find that
I'm most compatible with G-44s.

676
00:37:09.229 --> 00:37:10.813
and I don't mean to brag.

677
00:37:10.814 --> 00:37:14.525
but I usually sweep them
off their feet.

678
00:37:14.526 --> 00:37:16.068
I'll grab her legs.

679
00:37:16.069 --> 00:37:19.489
Let's get her to Dr. Morgan
before this wears off.

680
00:37:23.493 --> 00:37:26.453
Well. I guess everyone's
done playing nice.

681
00:37:26.454 --> 00:37:28.497
<i>Okay. listen up. team.</i>

682
00:37:28.498 --> 00:37:30.332
The moment we're out of FTL.

683
00:37:30.333 --> 00:37:32.584
the bridge will fire
an EM pulse at "Ark 22."

684
00:37:32.585 --> 00:37:34.545
Once we have confirmation
of a hit.

685
00:37:34.546 --> 00:37:36.255
we'll launch and board.

686
00:37:36.256 --> 00:37:39.550
We should expect
heavy resistance.

687
00:37:39.551 --> 00:37:41.760
<i>Bridge to Kimi...
we're two minutes out.</i>

688
00:37:41.761 --> 00:37:42.845
Are you ready?

689
00:37:42.846 --> 00:37:45.848
We're locked and loaded. bridge.

690
00:37:55.317 --> 00:37:57.067
Wow.

691
00:37:57.068 --> 00:37:59.403
You shouldn't be conscious.

692
00:37:59.404 --> 00:38:02.072
Our metabolism is fantastic.
isn't it?

693
00:38:02.073 --> 00:38:04.992
Triple the dosage
on the sedative.

694
00:38:07.746 --> 00:38:10.581
Don't worry.

695
00:38:10.582 --> 00:38:12.916
This won't hurt too much.

696
00:38:23.178 --> 00:38:26.138
Where's Garnet?

697
00:38:26.139 --> 00:38:28.933
-Medbay.
-Oh. yeah?

698
00:38:33.730 --> 00:38:36.440
-You don't have to do this.
-Yes. I do. You're the one.

699
00:38:36.441 --> 00:38:37.733
What does that mean?

700
00:38:39.486 --> 00:38:40.861
Shh.

701
00:38:40.862 --> 00:38:42.530
Go to sleep now.

702
00:38:44.616 --> 00:38:45.825
Sharon!

703
00:39:29.202 --> 00:39:30.412
Ian!

704
00:39:35.041 --> 00:39:37.377
Let's get the hell
off this ship.

705
00:39:39.087 --> 00:39:41.505
Sasha. you have a handle
on the EM pulse. right?

706
00:39:41.506 --> 00:39:43.132
-Yep.
-Good.

707
00:39:43.133 --> 00:39:45.009
Timing is everything on this.

708
00:39:45.010 --> 00:39:47.094
Leaving FTL

709
00:39:47.095 --> 00:39:50.723
in three. two. one...

710
00:39:50.724 --> 00:39:52.641
Fire EMP. Sasha.

711
00:39:52.642 --> 00:39:54.643
At what?

712
00:39:54.644 --> 00:39:56.854
There's no sign of "Ark 22."

713
00:39:56.855 --> 00:39:58.440
Oh. no.

714
00:40:01.318 --> 00:40:03.736
We can't get a visual
on "Ark 22."

715
00:40:03.737 --> 00:40:07.574
<i>We're too late.
"Ark 22" has left.</i>

716
00:40:13.705 --> 00:40:17.207
I asked you to do one thing.

717
00:40:17.208 --> 00:40:20.794
I know. I'm sorry.
I just saw red.

718
00:40:20.795 --> 00:40:22.880
That... that
can't happen again.

719
00:40:22.881 --> 00:40:25.132
It won't.
I-I promise.

720
00:40:25.133 --> 00:40:27.718
I need to handle this my way.

721
00:40:27.719 --> 00:40:30.095
I know.

722
00:40:30.096 --> 00:40:32.848
Last thing I would want
to do is hurt you.

723
00:40:32.849 --> 00:40:35.060
-Okay?
-Okay.

724
00:40:36.770 --> 00:40:39.188
Yeah. I'm sorry.

725
00:40:45.820 --> 00:40:49.531
Why are you looking
at Milan's file?

726
00:40:49.532 --> 00:40:52.159
I just wanted to see
who we're dealing with.

727
00:40:52.160 --> 00:40:55.579
<i>We</i> are not dealing with this.
<i>I</i> am.

728
00:40:55.580 --> 00:40:58.624
-Why can't you understand that?
-I do.

729
00:40:58.625 --> 00:41:00.667
I do. I'm s...

730
00:41:00.668 --> 00:41:01.752
Sanji.

731
00:41:01.753 --> 00:41:04.171
-I need some time alone.
-Oh. come on.

732
00:41:04.172 --> 00:41:05.589
I said I need some time.

733
00:41:05.590 --> 00:41:08.884
Or do I need to tell you
that twice. too?

734
00:41:11.596 --> 00:41:14.473
I tried to keep Felix
from searching too far

735
00:41:14.474 --> 00:41:18.602
from the settlement.
but he is determined

736
00:41:18.603 --> 00:41:21.522
to find Angus and Kelly.

737
00:41:21.523 --> 00:41:23.941
You need to take this
more seriously.

738
00:41:25.944 --> 00:41:28.779
I am taking this seriously.

739
00:41:28.780 --> 00:41:31.533
but there's nothing we can do.

740
00:41:33.410 --> 00:41:36.829
You could have stopped Felix
from searching further.

741
00:41:36.830 --> 00:41:41.041
Well. it's not like
he's gonna find the two kids.

742
00:41:41.042 --> 00:41:44.253
Ves. we both know
what happened to them.

743
00:41:44.254 --> 00:41:45.796
Do we?

744
00:41:45.797 --> 00:41:48.048
Because if you're right.

745
00:41:48.049 --> 00:41:50.676
we have a much bigger problem
than we thought.
